Now common utilities. 

`src/common/paths.ts`:
```ts
import { join } from 'path';
export const PUBLIC_DIR = join(process.cwd(),'public');
export const VIEWS_DIR = join(process.cwd(),'views');
export const POSTS_UPLOAD_DIR = join(PUBLIC_DIR,'images','blog');
...
```

`slug.ts`:
Use `slugify` transliterate. Could install `slugify` package, or write:
```ts
export function slugify(input: string): string {
 return input.normalize('NFD').replace(/[\u0300-\u036f]/g,'').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-').replace(/^-+|-+$/g,'');
}
```
Symfony AsciiSlugger also transliterates, lowercases, replaces non-alnum with '-'. Good. If empty, fallback 'item'.

`date-format.ts`: implement Twig-like formats used. We'll write function:
```ts
const MONTHS = [...];
const DAYS = [...];
export function formatDate(value: Date|string, format = 'd F Y'): string {
 const d = value instanceof Date ? value : new Date(value);
 if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return '';
 // Replace tokens
 const hours = d.getHours(); // local time
 const hours12 = hours % 12 || 12;
 const map: Record<string,string> = {
  'd': String(d.getDate()).padStart(2,'0'),
  'j': String(d.getDate()),
  'F': MONTHS[d.getMonth()],
  'M': MONTHS[d.getMonth()].slice(0,3),
  'm': String(d.getMonth()+1).padStart(2,'0'),
  'n': String(d.getMonth()+1),
  'Y': String(d.getFullYear()),
  'y': String(d.getFullYear()).slice(-2),
  'g': String(hours12),
  'h': String(hours12).padStart(2,'0'),
  'G': String(hours),
  'H': String(hours).padStart(2,'0'),
  'i': String(d.getMinutes()).padStart(2,'0'),
  's': String(d.getSeconds()).padStart(2,'0'),
  'A': hours < 12 ? 'AM':'PM',
  'a': hours < 12 ? 'am':'pm',
 };
 // Escape backslash? Simple token replacement character by character.
 return format.replace(/\\?[a-zA-Z]/g, (token) => { if(token.startsWith('\\')) return token.slice(1); return map[token] ?? token; });
}
```
Need careful: replacement for unknown letters returns token. Good. Nunjucks filter invocation `{{ date | date('d') }}` passes value and arg.

`view-helpers.ts`: asset:
```ts
export function asset(path: string): string {
 return '/' + String(path ?? '').replace(/^\/+/, '');
}
```

`csrf.service.ts`:
```ts
@Injectable()
export class CsrfService {
 token(req: Request): string { if (!req.session.csrfToken) req.session.csrfToken = randomBytes(32).toString('hex'); return req.session.csrfToken; }
 assertValid(req: Request): void {
   const sent = req.body?._csrf ?? req.body?._csrf_token;
   if (!sent || sent !== req.session?.csrfToken) throw new ForbiddenException('Token CSRF inválido o expirado');
 }
}
```
But `req.body` may be undefined. Fine.

Session augmentation `src/types/express-session.d.ts`:
```ts
import 'express-session';
import type { User } from '../entities/user.entity';
declare module 'express-session' {
 interface SessionData {
   userId?: number;
   csrfToken?: string;
   lastUsername?: string;
   flash?: { type:'success'|'error'|'info'; message:string } | null;
 }
}
declare global {
 namespace Express {
   interface Request { user?: User; }
 }
}
export {};
```
The global Express namespace augmentation in a module file with export {} works. But importing User type is okay.

Middleware:
```ts
@Injectable()
export class ViewerMiddleware implements NestMiddleware {
 constructor(private users: UsersService, private csrf: CsrfService) {}
 async use(req,res,next) {
   res.locals.currentPath = req.path;
   res.locals.currentUser = null;
   res.locals.flash = req.session?.flash ?? null;
   if (req.session) { delete req.session.flash; req.session.csrfToken = this.csrf.token(req); }
   res.locals.csrfToken = req.session?.csrfToken;
   if (req.session?.userId) { ... }
   next();
 }
}
```
Caveat: deleting flash then setting res.locals flash before delete is fine.
Using async middleware with Nest/Express 5: Nest supports async use returning Promise? Middleware interface `use(req,res,next): any`; Express 5 handles promise rejection but we call next. Fine.
`res.locals` type can accept any.
Need always call next even on DB error? try/catch next(error).

Guards:
`auth.guard.ts`:
```ts
@Injectable()
export class AuthGuard implements CanActivate {
 canActivate(ctx: ExecutionContext): boolean {
  const req = ctx.switchToHttp().getRequest<Request>();
  const res = ctx.switchToHttp().getResponse<Response>();
  if (req.user) return true;
  res.redirect('/login');
  return false;
 }
}
```
Since middleware sets req.user before guards. Yes, Nest middleware runs before guards.

`admin.guard.ts`:
```ts
if (!req.user) { res.redirect('/login'); return false; }
if (!req.user.isAdmin) throw new ForbiddenException('Acceso denegado');
return true;
```
Symfony access_control would redirect anonymous to login and 403 authenticated non-admin. Good.

`post-file.interceptor` config can be inline in controller. Create helper `createImageUploadInterceptor(field, destination)`? Let's make `src/common/upload.ts` exporting:
```ts
import { diskStorage } from 'multer';
import { extname, join } from 'path';
import { randomBytes } from 'crypto';
import { slugify } from './slug';
import { BadRequestException } from '@nestjs/common';

export const IMAGE_MIME_EXTENSIONS = { 'image/jpeg':'jpg', 'image/png':'png' };

export function imageStorage(destination: string) {
 return diskStorage({
  destination,
  filename: (req,file,cb) => {
    const base = slugify(file.originalname.replace(/\.[^.]+$/,'')) || 'imagen';
    const ext = IMAGE_MIME_EXTENSIONS[file.mimetype] ?? extname(file.originalname).replace('.','') ?? 'jpg';
    cb(null, `${base}-${Date.now().toString(16)}${randomBytes(4).toString('hex')}.${ext}`);
  }
 });
}
export function imageFileFilter(req,file,cb) {
 if (!IMAGE_MIME_EXTENSIONS[file.mimetype]) return cb(new BadRequestException('Por favor sube una imagen válida (JPEG o PNG)'), false);
 cb(null,true);
}
export async function removeFile(file?: Express.Multer.File) { if (file?.path) await unlink(file.path).catch(()=>undefined); }
```
