Now BlogController rewrite. Careful with route registration order. Also use `@Req` for single post.

Build pager for category path: basePath `/blog/categoria/${encodeURIComponent(slug)}`.

Search pager query mode.

Need to ensure `/blog/new` GET is before `/blog/:page`.

Validation for category optional in post creation? Let's make category required? Original posts didn't have. To be flexible, optional. But "categorías en posts" better required? Make optional to avoid blocking. Provide select with "Sin categoría".

Published checkbox: `formBoolean(req.body.published)`. Default checked in view.

Image on create required. On edit optional.

Tags form value: `tags: formString(req.body.tags)` for redisplay.

Post creation:
```ts
const categoryId = parseInteger(req.body.category, 0);
let category = null;
if (categoryId > 0) { category = await blogService.findCategoryById(categoryId); if(!category) errors.category='...'; }
```
If categoryId NaN? parseInteger returns NaN; Number.isNaN check -> error.

Handle CSRF error with removeUploadedFile.

After create:
```ts
const post = await this.blogService.createPost(..., req.user);
if (post.published) redirect single_post else redirect / (flash info)
```
But if non-admin draft, they can't manage. Could redirect `/blog/new` with flash "Borrador guardado. Un administrador puede publicarlo." Fine. Actually maybe better only admin can create drafts; if non-admin, force published=true regardless of checkbox? The view can hide checkbox for non-admin. Simpler: controller sets published only if user.isAdmin; non-admin always true. We'll do:
```ts
const published = req.user.isAdmin ? formBoolean(req.body.published) : true;
```
Same in admin edit.

Single post:
```ts
@Get('single_post/:slug')
async singlePost(@Param('slug') slug, @Req() req, @Res() res) {
 const includeDrafts = Boolean(req.user?.isAdmin);
 const post = await this.blogService.findBySlug(slug, includeDrafts);
 if (!post) throw new NotFoundException('Post no encontrado');
 const viewed = req.session.viewedPosts ?? [];
 if (!viewed.includes(post.id)) { req.session.viewedPosts=[...viewed, post.id]; await incrementViews; post.numViews=(post.numViews??0)+1; }
 const liked = await hasLiked(post.id, req.sessionID);
 const recents = await findRecents(5);
 const comments = (post.comments ?? []).filter(c=>c.approved || req.user?.isAdmin);
 res.render('blog/single_post',{post,comments,recents,liked,...});
}
```
Need `post.comments = comments` for view? Pass separate `comments`.

Comment POST:
- post = findBySlug(slug, true) because commenting on draft? Only published; use false. But admin can see drafts; commenting draft weird. Use includeDrafts false for public.
- honeypot `website`.
- validation then render single post with errors. Need helper renderSinglePost with req/res. Create private method.
- addComment with req.ip.
- flash, redirect.

Rendering single post helper signature handles post loading, liked, viewed increments? For error redisplay shouldn't increment again. Simpler: fetch post, fetch recents, hasLiked, filter comments, render. Separate `renderSinglePost(req,res,slug,{commentValues,commentErrors,post?})`. For GET, handle view increment before render.

Let's write carefully.

Like endpoint:
- `@Get('single_post/:slug/like')` toggle, redirect back. However guests have session id; fine.
- `@Post` toggle, json.
Need `sessionID` available on Request type (express-session adds). Yes.

CSRF for GET like? no.

