Now main.ts. Include:
- helmet
- session store
- rate limiting
- global filter
- fallback
- session cleanup
- trust proxy

Need `getRepositoryToken` from @nestjs/typeorm, `Repository` from typeorm, Session entity.
`import { Request, Response, NextFunction } from 'express'`.
`import { Logger } from '@nestjs/common'`.
`AllExceptionsFilter`.

Order:
```ts
const app = await NestFactory.create<NestExpressApplication>(AppModule);
const config = app.get(ConfigService);
app.set('trust proxy', 1);
app.use(helmet({...}));
// nunjucks
app.useStaticAssets(PUBLIC_DIR);
// session
const sessionRepository = app.get<Repository<Session>>(getRepositoryToken(Session));
const store = new TypeOrmSessionStore(sessionRepository);
app.use(session({... store ...}));
// rate limits
...
// viewer
app.use((req,res,next)=>viewer.use(req,res,next));
app.useGlobalFilters(new AllExceptionsFilter());
await app.init();
// fallback & error handler
const expressApp = app.getHttpAdapter().getInstance();
expressApp.use((req,res)=> {...404...});
expressApp.use((err,req,res,next)=>{...500...});
// cleanup interval
setInterval(()=>void store.clearExpired().catch(()=>undefined), 60*60*1000).unref();
await app.listen(port);
```
Note `app.useGlobalFilters` can be before init. Good.

Potential issue: Nunjucks `express: app.getHttpAdapter().getInstance()` references the express app; render works in middleware fallback. Yes.

Error handler for fallback uses res.render; if error occurs during render, express error handler might loop; guard with headersSent.

404 fallback: render 'errors/404' with status/message; ensure `res.locals` has csrf etc from viewer middleware (registered before). For unmatched route, viewer middleware runs. Good.

Rate limiter placement: before viewer? If limit triggers and renders error view, csrfToken may be undefined -> base uses `csrfToken` maybe only in forms; error view extends base without forms. Fine. But base references currentUser, currentPath — undefined okay in Nunjucks? `currentUser` undefined is falsy. currentPath undefined fine. It may reference flash undefined fine. So rate limiter before viewer works. But for rendered 429, base nav active checks `currentPath == '/'` false. Fine. Better put viewer before rate limit so locals exist. Session middleware must be before viewer; rate can be after viewer. Order: session -> viewer -> rate limit -> routes. The viewer sets csrf token and current user then rate limit 429 has full context. Global post limiter after viewer. Do that.

But viewer is async DB call for user each request; rate limit after means abusive requests still hit DB. Fine for this app. Or rate before viewer; error page needs no user. I'll put rate immediately after session, before viewer, to protect DB. Error page renders base; currentUser undefined acceptable. But Nunjucks autoescape undefined -> empty. Good.

`app.use(['/login', ...], onPost(...))` — Express types support PathParams; TypeScript may complain array of strings is fine.

Regex: `app.use(/^\/reset-password\/[^/]+$/, onPost(authLimiter));` TS type RegExp accepted.

Global post limiter: `app.use(onPost(rateLimit({ windowMs: 10*60*1000, max: 120, keyPrefix: 'global-post' })))` — app.use(handler) fine.

Could global limiter interfere with likes toggling tests (max 120)? Fine.

Session cleanup interval only after store created.

Helmet CSP disabled for inline scripts.

`app.useStaticAssets(PUBLIC_DIR)` before session means static requests skip session/rate/viewer. Good.

Fallback 404 must be after init. But note `app.listen` maybe calls init again (no-op). Good.

Need `app.getHttpAdapter().getInstance()` returns any.

Let's write.

